// ItemAttachment is the Schema for the ItemAttachments API. This resource attaches a file to an item, in the personal vault of the provider user or in an organization. The file is encrypted like Bitwarden clients do: with its own attachment key, which is encrypted with the key of the item. Attachments cannot be changed: a different content or file name replaces the attachment. Changes to the content are detected with its SHA-256 hash (content_sha256), so changing only the path of file keeps the attachment. Empty files are not supported. Use the vaultwarden_item_attachment ephemeral resource to read the content of an attachment. Vaultwarden limits the storage of attachments with USER_ATTACHMENT_LIMIT and ORG_ATTACHMENT_LIMIT, and accepts files up to 525 MB. Requires email and master_password to be set in the provider configuration.
